{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791447961,"nonce":"wOw0K3h7AMOwsHkisoEShdxlwCw=","message":"Reproduced numeric variant slot mismatch on 3757f9771dd11f95baf18fbdb0758eba0f089d7d.\n\n/tmp/VariantSlotProbe.hx has f(Int):Float overridden by f(Float):Float and variant(Int):Float overridden by variant(Float):Int. Native Haxe outputs 42,42.5,1,1 (/tmp/rayzor-variant-slots-native-v1.log). Pinned Cranelift returns an enormous stale Float for both calls through SlotParent, while calls through SlotChild return 42.5 and 1 (/tmp/rayzor-variant-slots-before-v1.log).\n\nThe fractional child call is important: blindly forcing every caller argument through the introducing Int signature would truncate 41.5 and violate native behavior. Any slot adapter must preserve that child-call behavior while adapting the base Int call and the Int implementation result consumed as Float. A common widened numeric slot ABI is one possible design; do not assume introducing-method casts alone are sufficient.\n\nCurrent ensure_vtable_dispatch_thunk in decl/vtables.rs builds its ABI from the implementing function and prepends env. try_virtual_dispatch builds its indirect signature from passed registers and expr.ty. Class virtual_dispatch_info records the implementation's class rather than a canonical slot declaration. Interface slots also reuse thunks keyed only by the implementation IrFunctionId, though their declared signature may differ. These are the shared paths to investigate for Issue9836, TestInterface and Issue8528; no fix or score gain claimed yet.","files":null}]}